---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: All the claims
description: "Every claim on file, verbatim, with the context it was cut from and the five layers of ENTIA it is read through: from the literature and from the research log."
permalink: /en/claims/all/
lang: en
bodyClass: claims-page
og_card: /images/og/og-en-home.png
---
{# ===================================================================
   /en/claims/all/ — l'elenco completo (13/11/2026).
   In testa la matrice alla Bertin, a piena giustezza: e' la chiave di
   lettura (un clic su una colonna porta all'unita', un clic su un
   concetto filtra). Sotto, il registro a piena giustezza, nell'ordine
   della matrice: Tema, Argomento, concetto, peso. Sul telefono la matrice
   si gira: una riga per claim, cinque celle.
   Ogni unita' ha l'ancora del suo id (i link /en/claims/all/#id restano
   validi). Contesto e tagli si aprono a richiesta; senza JavaScript si
   vede tutto. Dati: src/_data/claimPages.js.
   =================================================================== #}
{% set P = claimPages %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/carota.css">
{% set MARK = { point: "•", therefore: "∴", exists: "∃", directive: "!" } %}

<p class="cp-k"><a href="/en/claims/">Claims</a> › All the claims</p>
<h1 class="cp-h1">All the claims</h1>
<p class="cp-lede">Every claim on file, verbatim, with the context it was cut from and the five layers it is read through. The paraphrase is mine; the quotation is theirs.</p>
<p class="al-meta">{{ P.counts.claims }} claims · {{ P.counts.concepts }} concepts · {{ P.counts.relations }} declared relations · in the order of the matrix: theme, topic, concept, weight</p>

<section class="al-mx" id="matrix" aria-labelledby="matrix-h">
  <p class="cp-k" id="matrix-h">The claims, tabulated</p>
  <p class="al-cap">One column per claim, one row per value of each layer, the relations as arcs above. Click a column to read the claim below; click a concept to see only its claims.</p>
  <div class="al-mxd">{{ P.matrix | safe }}</div>
  <p class="al-leg">{% for f in claims.FAMIGLIE %}<span><b>{{ MARK[f.forma] }}</b> {{ f.en }}</span>{% endfor %}<span><b class="lit">●</b> from the literature</span><span><b class="log">●</b> from the research log</span><span><b class="ring">◯</b> contested, weighted ×1.5</span></p>

  {# sul telefono: la matrice girata, una riga per claim #}
  <div class="al-strip" aria-label="The claims, one row each">
    <p class="al-sh"><span>Claim</span><span>1 Name</span><span>4 Concept</span><span>5</span></p>
    {% for t in P.themes %}
    <p class="al-st">{{ t.en }}</p>
    {% for tp in t.topics %}
    <p class="al-sto">{{ tp.en }}</p>
    {% for c in tp.claims %}
    <a class="al-sr al-{{ c.voice }}" href="#{{ c.id }}"><span class="n">{{ c.n }}</span><span class="c1">{{ c.names[0] if c.names.length else "" }}</span><span class="c4">{{ c.conceptsEn[0].en }}{% if c.conceptsEn.length > 1 %} +{% endif %}</span><span class="c5"><i style="width:{{ (c.w / 2 * 100) | round }}%"></i></span></a>
    {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<div class="al-bar" id="al-bar">
  <p class="cp-k">Read by kind of warrant</p>
  <div class="al-fn">
    <button type="button" data-fn="" aria-pressed="true">All <b>{{ P.counts.claims }}</b></button>
    {% for f in claims.FAMIGLIE %}{% set nn = P.counts.shapes[f.forma] %}{% if nn %}<button type="button" data-fn="{{ f.forma }}" aria-pressed="false"><span>{{ MARK[f.forma] }}</span> {{ f.en }} <b>{{ nn }}</b></button>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="al-now" id="al-now" hidden><span></span> <button type="button" id="al-clear">Show all the claims</button></p>
</div>

<div class="al-reg" id="al-reg">
{% for t in P.themes %}
<section class="rg-th" data-theme="{{ t.key }}">
  <h2>{{ t.en }}</h2>
  <p>{{ t.position }}</p>
  {% for tp in t.topics %}
  <h3 class="rg-to">{{ tp.en }} <span>{{ tp.claims.length }}</span></h3>
  {% for c in tp.claims %}
  <article class="u u-{{ c.voice }}" id="{{ c.id }}" data-fn="{{ c.shape }}" data-concepts="{{ c.concepts | join(' ') }}">
    <div class="u-l">
      <a class="u-n" href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.n }}</a><span class="u-m" title="{{ c.d1 }}">{{ MARK[c.shape] }}{% if c.contested %}<i>contested</i>{% endif %}</span>
      <ol class="u-st">
        <li class="s1"><b>1</b> {{ c.names | join(" · ") if c.names.length else "—" }}</li>
        <li class="s2"><b>2</b> {{ c.topicEn }}</li>
        <li class="s3"><b>3</b> {{ c.themeEn }}</li>
        <li class="s4"><b>4</b> {% for k in c.conceptsEn %}<a href="{{ k.url }}">{{ k.en }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} + {% endif %}{% endfor %}</li>
        <li class="s5"><b>5</b> <span class="w"><i style="width:{{ (c.w / 2 * 100) | round }}%"></i></span> {{ c.w }}</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="u-r">
      <p class="u-g">{{ c.gist }}</p>
      {% if c.before %}<p class="u-ctx">&hellip;{{ c.before }}</p>{% endif %}
      <blockquote{% if c.doi %} cite="https://doi.org/{{ c.doi }}"{% endif %}>&ldquo;{% for part in c.parts %}{{ part }}{% if not loop.last %}<span class="u-gap"><span class="u-ell">[&hellip;]</span><span class="u-cut">{{ c.cuts[loop.index0] }}</span></span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}&rdquo;</blockquote>
      {% if c.after %}<p class="u-ctx">{{ c.after }}&hellip;</p>{% endif %}
      <p class="u-act">{% if c.before or c.after %}<button type="button" class="u-pass">The passage</button>{% endif %}{% if c.cuts.length %}<button type="button" class="u-cuts">The cuts</button>{% endif %}<a href="{{ c.url }}">Its page &#8594;</a></p>
      <p class="u-src">{% if c.voice == "literature" %}In their own words{% else %}From the research log{% endif %} · {% if c.doi %}<a href="https://doi.org/{{ c.doi }}" rel="external">{{ c.cite }}</a>{% elif c.voice == "log" %}<a href="{{ c.src }}">{{ c.cite }}</a>{% else %}{{ c.cite }}{% endif %}{% if c.locus %} · {{ c.locus }}{% endif %} · {{ c.stance }} · {{ c.fn }} · {{ c.d1 }}{% if c.d1Label %} {{ c.d1Label }}{% endif %}{% if c.d1Status != "confirmed" %}?{% endif %}</p>
      {% if c.out.length %}<ul class="u-rel">{% for r in c.out %}<li><span class="how">{{ r.how }} →</span> <a href="#{{ r.id }}">{{ r.n }}</a> <em>{{ r.why }}</em></li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </article>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
</section>
{% endfor %}
</div>

<section class="cp-sec al-how" aria-labelledby="how">
  <h2 id="how">How to read a unit</h2>
  <p><strong>The paraphrase is mine.</strong> It opens each unit, in sans, and says what the claim holds and why it is here. It is not the source speaking.</p>
  <p><strong>The quotation is theirs.</strong> Everything in the ruled block is verbatim. Where it skips something the gap is marked, and the omitted words can be put back: a cut you cannot inspect is an argument you have to take on trust.</p>
  <p class="al-small">{{ P.counts.claims }} claims from {{ claims.FONTI }} sources, {{ claims.D1N.length }} of 11 D1 codes, {{ claims.FN.length }} of 6 <a href="/en/entia/#functions">ENTIA functions</a>. A question mark on a D1 code means it is proposed and not yet confirmed by hand. The five layers, the rule for choosing a claim and the weight formula are on the <a href="/en/entia/#claims">ENTIA page</a>; the same set as one document is <a href="/en/claims/#ledger">The Claims Ledger</a>.</p>
</section>

<script src="/js/elenco.js" defer></script>
